      {
        "index": 3,
        "text": "Shortly afterwards, the media published a conservative argument objecting to cloning owing to moral problems, and suggested the constitution include compulsory regulations to forbid obtaining commercial profits from cloning. When interviewed, the scientist stared at the decorations on the ceiling, thinking for a while, and then said, “I’m not in favour of any arbitrary assumption, but undertaking cloning does differ from the straightforward procedure of making loaves out of flour. Until we accumulate enough exact knowledge, any practice is in vain and is bound to fail.",
        "zh": "不久后，媒体出于道德问题发表了反对克隆的保守观点，并建议宪法纳入强制性规定，禁止通过克隆获取商业利润。接受采访时，科学家盯着天花板上的装饰，想了一会儿，然后说：“我不赞成任何武断的假设，但开展克隆确实不同，不同于用面粉制作面包那样直接明了的过程。在积累足够准确的知识之前，任何尝试都是徒劳的，注定会失败。",
        "start": 99.61333333333333,
        "voiceEnd": 144.14333333333332,
        "end": 188.67333333333335,
